<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador monetary base up 7.46 pct in October.</title>
<headline>Ecuador monetary base up 7.46 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base grew 7.46 percent to 2.75 billion sucres in October, the Central Bank said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In September, money base grew 0.87 percent to 2.56 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The bank gave no reason for the increase.</p>
<p>In the first ten months of 1996, the monetary base increased 38.3 percent.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
